From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 21:51:23 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 10197/11362] Private tmp base per pytest invocation: runs can
 no longer destroy each other

REQ-HARNESS-5930 (spec added with this change; the incident is quoted there).

WHY. pyproject pins tmp_path_retention_count = 1 and every invocation shared
pytest's default rotation root (/tmp/pytest-of-<user>). Each new pytest pruned
the numbered bases down to the retention count -- including a still-running
job's. The conductor runs pytest every few minutes, so two ~8h full-suite
measurement runs were destroyed mid-flight, and the damage was worse than
lost wall clock: mid-run deletion turned real failures into setup errors,
SUPPRESSING the failure count those runs existed to measure (this is why
ops/global_suite_failure_baseline.json had to be taken from "run 3, private
--basetemp" -- the only uncontaminated measurement).

THE FIX. tests/python/conftest.py assigns every invocation with no explicit
--basetemp a fresh private base under /tmp/pytest-carnot-<user>/ (timestamp +
pid + random suffix). With an explicit base pytest never rotates numbered
dirs and never prunes siblings, so the deletion vector is gone rather than
mitigated. An explicit --basetemp is respected untouched; xdist workers
arrive with a controller-assigned subdirectory and are untouched too. Stale
sibling bases older than a day are pruned best-effort -- age-based, so a
live run (full suite ~4h) can never be collected.

THE WIRING PROOF HAD TO BE WORKER-PROOF, and the first version was not:
pytest-xdist hands each worker <session_base>/popen-gwN even when the
controller had NO basetemp, so "assert basetemp is set" passes vacuously in
workers -- discovered when the delete-the-wiring mutation stayed GREEN. The
committed test normalizes to the session base and asserts it does not live
under the shared pytest-of-<user> rotation root, which turns that mutation
RED under the default -n 4 invocation.

Mutation-proved, 4 rules: uniqueness gutted (constant name) RED; explicit
basetemp overridden RED; prune ignoring age (would collect live runs) RED;
conftest wiring deleted RED. 6/6 after restore; neighbouring suites
(operator-curated-doc guard, harness lint, conductor narrowing, mutation
check) all green alongside.

Registered in qa_layer_authenticity_audit.py ACKNOWLEDGED_NON_QA_LAYER with
the reason written out: isolation infrastructure whose failure loses a
measurement run, not a guard whose failure admits a false claim -- and its
name carries no guard marker, so nothing else would have recorded the
decision. --check-targets OK, audit suite 79/79.

